WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.689
Elena’s coworker shows her a brochure: two hundred dollars a

00:00:03.689 --> 00:00:07.378
day while in the hospital, for forty dollars a month.

00:00:07.378 --> 00:00:08.853
Is that health insurance?

00:00:08.853 --> 00:00:09.222
No.

00:00:09.222 --> 00:00:11.067
It is a limited policy.

00:00:11.067 --> 00:00:16.231
Limited policies restrict either the perils they cover, such as accidents only, or the

00:00:16.231 --> 00:00:21.027
amounts they pay, such as a fixed daily sum unrelated to the bill.

00:00:21.027 --> 00:00:23.609
They are useful supplements and poor substitutes.

00:00:23.609 --> 00:00:28.036
Because buyers so often mistake them for comprehensive coverage, the policy must

00:00:28.036 --> 00:00:32.462
carry a prominent notice, typically on the first page, stating that it

00:00:32.462 --> 00:00:36.520
is a limited policy and describing what it does not cover.

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:41.173
An accident-only policy pays for injuries from accidents and nothing for sickness.

00:00:41.173 --> 00:00:45.439
It may pay medical expenses, a disability income benefit, or AD

00:00:45.439 --> 00:00:49.316
and D sums, but the trigger is always an accident.

00:00:49.316 --> 00:00:53.582
A specified disease, or dread disease, policy pays only on diagnosis

00:00:53.582 --> 00:00:57.847
of the named illness, most often cancer, and usually pays scheduled

00:00:57.847 --> 00:01:01.337
or lump-sum amounts regardless of what other coverage pays.

00:01:01.337 --> 00:01:06.766
Rosa might buy a cancer policy to cover travel and lost income during treatment.

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:09.868
She must still carry a medical plan for

00:01:09.868 --> 00:01:12.970
everything else, and Theo must say so plainly.

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:16.366
A hospital indemnity policy pays a fixed amount for each

00:01:16.366 --> 00:01:19.762
day the insured is confined, regardless of the actual charges,

00:01:19.762 --> 00:01:22.818
which is why it is sometimes called hospital income.

00:01:22.818 --> 00:01:25.535
It helps with deductibles and lost pay but

00:01:25.535 --> 00:01:27.912
does not cover physician or outpatient bills.

00:01:27.912 --> 00:01:30.629
Credit disability insurance pays the installments on a

00:01:30.629 --> 00:01:33.006
specific loan while the borrower is disabled.

00:01:33.006 --> 00:01:36.402
The creditor is the beneficiary, the benefit cannot exceed the

00:01:36.402 --> 00:01:39.798
debt, and the premium is often added to the loan.

00:01:39.798 --> 00:01:43.194
When Dennis finances a car, he may be offered credit

00:01:43.194 --> 00:01:46.250
disability; he may decline it without losing the loan.

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:49.724
Priya sponsors a softball team and buys blanket accident coverage.

00:01:49.724 --> 00:01:53.546
Blanket insurance covers a changing group of people exposed to a

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:57.368
common hazard without naming each one: a team’s players, passengers on

00:01:57.368 --> 00:02:01.190
a bus, students at a school, campers at a summer camp.

00:02:01.190 --> 00:02:04.317
No individual certificates are issued because the members change.

00:02:04.317 --> 00:02:08.139
Benefits usually pay medical expenses from accidents during the covered activity.

00:02:08.139 --> 00:02:13.003
Blanket coverage is group coverage in form, but it insures a category of people

00:02:13.003 --> 00:02:17.520
rather than enrolled individuals, and that difference is the point the exam tests.

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:23.183
Separate vision plans cover eye care, and drug plans cover the prescriptions they list.

00:02:23.183 --> 00:02:26.823
A critical illness policy pays a lump sum for

00:02:26.823 --> 00:02:30.059
a listed diagnosis after any required survival period.

00:02:30.059 --> 00:02:34.508
You can use that money for rent, travel or another expense.

00:02:34.508 --> 00:02:38.957
Some limited benefits qualify for an exception to federal coverage rules.

00:02:38.957 --> 00:02:41.384
Separate limited vision benefits can qualify.

00:02:41.384 --> 00:02:46.642
So can independent critical illness coverage that does not coordinate with another plan.

00:02:46.642 --> 00:02:50.686
The exam term is excepted benefits: E, as in exception.

00:02:50.686 --> 00:02:55.540
A drug policy does not qualify just because it covers only prescriptions.

00:02:55.540 --> 00:03:01.073
Short-term limited duration policies bridge gaps, such as the weeks between jobs.

00:03:01.073 --> 00:03:07.528
They are medically underwritten, exclude pre-existing conditions and need not include essential health benefits.

00:03:07.528 --> 00:03:13.983
Federal rules allow longer terms, but Maryland is stricter: a short-term policy sold in

00:03:13.983 --> 00:03:20.437
Maryland may last less than three months and may not be renewed or extended.

00:03:20.437 --> 00:03:25.048
Theo’s client who leaves a job in May should compare

00:03:25.048 --> 00:03:29.659
a short-term plan with a special enrollment on Maryland Health

00:03:29.659 --> 00:03:33.808
Connection or Maryland continuation coverage, which provide comprehensive benefits.

00:03:33.808 --> 00:03:38.880
Short-term coverage is a stopgap, and the notice must say so.
